# Build context filter for every image in docker/ (all of them use the repo
# root as context, because they build workspace packages).
#
# Two reasons this file matters beyond build speed:
#
#  1. Secrets. A developer checkout has config.yaml, .env, and agent.db sitting
#     at the root. None are needed to build anything, and anything present in
#     the context can be baked into a layer by a careless COPY. Keep them out
#     of the context and that class of mistake stops being possible.
#  2. Size. .worktrees/ can hold dozens of full checkouts and node_modules is
#     multi-gigabyte; without this, every build uploads all of it to the daemon
#     before running the first instruction.

# ── Dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the image) ────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
ui-dist/
**/ui-dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.next/
**/.next/

# ── VCS and agent scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.worktrees/
.claude/

# ── Local instance state — secrets live here ────────────────────────────────
config.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
data/
docker/trusted-actions/data/
docker/trusted-actions/secrets/
docker/trusted-actions/screenshots/

# ── Not part of any runtime image ───────────────────────────────────────────
packages/site/
packages/integration-tests/
docs/
workflows/
*.md
!README.md
.changeset/
